SUMMARY:Reading Time with Ms. Chloe
DESCRIPTION:Registration Required. To schedule a time\, go to: Make an 
 Appointment - DCoL Events & Room Reservations - Durham County 
 Library\n\nDoes your child need more reading practice and could benefit 
 from more reading aloud time? Or are they just learning phonics sounds and 
 need more practice to build blending skills? Then this program is for them! 
 Schedule a 20-minute session for your child with Ms. Chloe to work together 
 with your child on reading and blending practice. You’re welcome to bring 
 your own book or I’ll pull some books that will work for their range. 
 \n\nWhile parents/ guardians don’t have to attend\, they must remain on 
 the children’s floor while their child is attending their session.\n\nFor 
 more information\, contact: chloebullock@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Main Library - Children's Area\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chloe Bullock":MAILTO:chloebullock@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-16591869
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16591869
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260602T213000Z
DTEND:20260602T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260602T000000Z
SUMMARY:CANCELLED SCORE presents: Welcome to Entrepreneurship
DESCRIPTION:You MUST register via SCORE's registration link: Welcome To 
 Entrepreneurship | SCORE\n\nLast opportunity to take this class until fall! 
 \n\n \n\nDuring this two hour in-person session you will learn 
 about:\n\n\n	Personal characteristics of an Entrepreneur\n	Legal 
 entities—LLC vs. Sole Proprietorship \n	Federal ID Number\n	Business 
 Feasibility Analysis\n	Capital—Equity vs. Debt\n	Basic Bookkeeping Made 
 Easy\n	Business Modeling\n	Insurance\n	Taxes—Filing requirements for 
 Federal and State\n\n\nLastly\, you will be introduced to SCORE and the 
 invaluable work that their Mentors provide to new start-ups.\n\nThe class 
 will be presented by Mr. Fred Lorber\, a certified SCORE mentor and class 
 instructor.\n\nMr. Lorber is a seasoned entrepreneur\, business development 
 expert\, and accomplished speaker with over three decades of experience in 
 sales\, strategic planning\, and customer relationship 
 management.\n\nLorber’s areas of expertise include new business 
 development\, strategic planning\, B2B sales\, and negotiation\, all honed 
 through a diverse career that spans industries such as e-commerce\, website 
 development\, hospitality\, and retail. Mr. Lorber has consistently 
 delivered results\, including growing businesses from start-up to 
 profitability\, improving customer engagement metrics\, and training teams 
 to achieve operational excellence.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jana Bradley":MAILTO:jbradley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development, Low Sensory Stimulation
UID:LibCal-14288-15430217
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15430217
END:VEVENT
