BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260603T220000Z
DTEND:20260603T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260603T000000Z
SUMMARY:Award Winning Insights with Juju Chang
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\nJoin us for an engaging conversation with Juju Chang\, 
 Emmy\, Peabody\, DuPont\, and Murrow Award-winning journalist and co-anchor 
 of ABC News’ Nightline.\n\nDrawing on over three decades of reporting on 
 national and international stories\, Chang will share insights from her 
 career\, her experiences in the newsroom\, and the art of storytelling that 
 connects with audiences everywhere.\n\n\n\n \n\nJuju Chang is an Emmy 
 Award-winning co-anchor of ABC News’ Nightline and a regular contributor 
 to Good Morning America and 20/20. An ABC News veteran\, she joined the 
 network as an honors graduate from Stanford University and has since held 
 nearly every pivotol role in broadcast news\, from producer for World News 
 Tonight to news anchor for Good Morning America. Throughout her thirty-year 
 career\, she has traveled the globe to report on the most pressing stories 
 of our time\, including natural disasters\, terrorism\, and international 
 breaking news. Known for her sophisticated long-form storytelling and 
 in-depth personal narratives\, Chang has conducted high-profile interviews 
 with a diverse range of newsmakers\, from heads of state and tech moguls to 
 icons of the entertainment industry. Her distinguished body of work has 
 been recognized with the industry’s highest honors\, including multiple 
 Emmy\, Gracie\, DuPont\, Murrow\, and Peabody Awards. Beyond the anchor 
 desk\, she is a member of the Council on Foreign Relations and a founding 
 board member of the Korean American Community Foundation.\n\n\nThis event 
 is brought to you by Durham County library Humanities\n\n \n\nand Sponsored 
 by Durham Library Foundation\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWhere can I park when the Main 
 Library parking lot is full?\n\nParking is available in the library parking 
 lot or at the North Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street 
 which is behind the apartments directly across the street from the library. 
 Parking is free in the garage. Please bring your ticket to a service desk 
 in the library for validation.\n\n
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
