SUMMARY:Leveraging Personal & Business Credit
DESCRIPTION:Are you preparing to make major financial decisions such as 
 securing funding\, purchasing equipment\, expanding operations\, acquiring 
 property\, or scaling your business? In 2026\, both personal and business 
 credit plays a critical role in determining access to capital\, loan 
 terms\, interest rates\, and overall financial positioning. This session is 
 designed for entrepreneurs and small business owners who are seeking to 
 strengthen their financial profile before making significant 
 investments.\n\nParticipants will learn the difference between personal and 
 business credit\, how lenders evaluate both\, and when each is used in 
 funding decisions. The training will cover personal credit optimization\, 
 business credit building strategies\, and how to align both profiles to 
 improve approval odds and funding capacity. The session will also discuss 
 current credit reporting agencies\, credit tiers\, utilization strategies\, 
 and how to avoid common mistakes that impact borrowing power.\n\nThis 
 session is ideal for business owners preparing for large financial moves 
 and those seeking to become funding-ready. By the end of the training\, 
 participants will understand how to leverage personal and business credit 
 together to support growth\, reduce risk\, and make informed financial 
 decisions.\n\nThis workshop is hosted by La-Tasha Best-Gaddy\, founder and 
 chief strategist of Infinity Bridges Inc. As a strategic visionary\, 
 La-Tasha is dedicated to creating infrastructure that generates legacy\, 
 not just income. She has spent decades building systems for small 
 businesses\, municipalities\, nonprofits\, and financial institutions\, 
 bridging technical expertise with practical strategy to elevate communities 
 often underestimated or excluded.
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development, Finance
UID:LibCal-14288-16705879
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16705879
END:VEVENT
