DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260608
DTSTAMP:20260607T000000Z
SUMMARY:Maker   STEAM Take and Make: DIY Scrap Dino Puppet
DESCRIPTION:In this month's Maker   STEAM Take and Make\, you'll find all 
 the recycled and reused materials from The Scrap Exchange to make your own 
 dino puppet! All you need is some adhesive and your creativity to complete 
 this kit at home. Thanks to The Scrap Exchange for compiling this 
 kit!\n\nKits are located in the shelving unit outside of the Innovation Lab 
 on the Third Floor at Main Library for you to take home and 
 complete.\n\nFirst come\, first serve while supplies last.
LOCATION:Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Environmental, Innovation Lab, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-16934955
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16934955
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260607T133000Z
DTEND:20260607T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260607T000000Z
SUMMARY:Roaming Readers: A Walking Audiobook Club!
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we walk the trails of RTP while listening to 
 audiobooks! After\, feel free to join us at Drift Coffee Shop & Kitchen RTP 
 for an optional discussion about the book and a chance to meet new 
 people.\n\n \n\nThis month’s suggested audiobook is Gay the Pray Away by 
 Natalie Naudus (available on Hoopla). If you have already read it\, or 
 would prefer another title\, we suggest: Queer as Folklore by Sacha Coward 
 (available on Hoopla) or My Darling Dreadful Thing by Johanna Van Veen 
 (available on Hoopla). \n\n \n\nThis event is for book lovers\, the 
 book-curious\, people who haven’t been able to make time to read (or 
 listen) for fun\, introverts\, extroverts\, exercisers\, caregivers pushing 
 strollers\, (leashed) dog owners\, groups\, singles\, nature lovers\, and 
 multi-taskers!\n\n \n\nAll paces welcome\, please take breaks when you need 
 them. We know it is easy to get transported to another world when listening 
 to your book. Be sure to stay alert as we will be crossing roads and may 
 encounter uneven pavement. \n\n \n\nWhile attendance is free\, please 
 register here to receive reminders and stay in the know for any updates. 
 Free public parking is located on the deck just across the street at 3150 
 Elion Drive. We will meet at 3151 Elion Drive Durham\, NC 27713.\n\n 
 \n\nQuestions? Email Elle at kfarmer@dconc.gov.\n\n \n\nUpcoming 
 dates:\n\nJuly 12th\n\nAugust 9th\n\nSeptember 13th\n\n
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Elle F.":MAILTO:kfarmer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Health & Fitness, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16545989
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16545989
END:VEVENT
