BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260608T220000Z
DTEND:20260608T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260608T000000Z
SUMMARY:Back to the Prairie-Little House for Adults
DESCRIPTION:Have you never read the Little House series by Laura Ingalls 
 Wilder and always wondered what the hype was about?  Did you read the 
 series as a child and wonder if these books hold up to an adult eye?  Come 
 join our Little House for adults book club! \n\nEach month will be a 
 different book from the series\, with our last meeting being a discussion 
 of the non fiction biography Prairie Fires by Caroline Fraser. \n\nAs this 
 book club will be discussing sensitive topics and issues\, no one under 18 
 will be allowed to attend.\n\nReading order\n\nSeptember-Little House in 
 the Big Woods\n\nOctober- Farmer Boy\n\nNovember- Little House on the 
 Prairie\n\nDecember- On The Banks of Plum Creek\n\nJanuary- By the Shores 
 of Silver Lake\n\nFebruary- The Long Winter\n\nMarch- Little Town on the 
 Prairie\n\nApril- These Happy Golden Years\n\nMay- The First Four 
 Years\n\nJune- Prairie Fires
LOCATION:Adult Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Laura B.":MAILTO:lbroadwater@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-14234580
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/14234580
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260608T220000Z
DTEND:20260608T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260608T000000Z
SUMMARY:From Idea to Enterprise: Library Tools for Entrepreneurs
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're thinking of starting a business or have an 
 established business\, the library has something for you -- in fact\, your 
 library card might be your most valuable business tool!\n\nLearn more about 
 Durham County Library's business\, entrepreneurship and investing resources 
 and information during this hour-long primer. \n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Meeting Room #4347\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jana Bradley":MAILTO:jbradley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development
UID:LibCal-14288-16039252
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16039252
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260608T223000Z
DTEND:20260608T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260608T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mystery Book Club -- Dark August
DESCRIPTION:Join us virtually\, or in person\, this month to discuss Dark 
 August by Katie Trello.\n\nAugusta (Gus) Monet is living an aimless 
 existence with her grifter boyfriend when she learns that her great 
 grandmother -- her last living relative -- has just died. Ditching her 
 boyfriend\, Gus returns to the home she left as a young girl. While combing 
 through her great grandmother's possessions\, Gus stumbles across an old 
 trunk filled with long-lost childhood belongings. She also discovers cold 
 case files that belonged to her mother\, a disgraced police detective who 
 died in a car accident when Gus was eight.\nIs Gus ready to learn the 
 truths that culminated on one terrible August night\, more than a decade 
 earlier\, when lives were taken\, and secrets were presumed buried 
 forever?\n\nClick here for format availability from the Durham 
 library.\n\nPhysical copies will be available at the North Regional 
 Information Desk while supplies last.\n\nRegistration is required to 
 receive the Zoom link to attend the event.\n\nE-mail Bob with any 
 questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-15134859
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15134859
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260608T230000Z
DTEND:20260609T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260608T000000Z
SUMMARY:Paleontology Trivia Night at Atomic Clock Brewery
DESCRIPTION:Join Durham County Library to prepare for Summer Reading 2026 
 with a blast from the past trivia night on fossils\, ancient creatures\, 
 and all things paleontology! Winners will receive an extra special Durham 
 County Library prize\, as well as bragging rights for all time. Teams are 
 limited to 8 people per team. \n\nRegistration is required. This program is 
 for adults only.\n\nThis is a special offsite event at Atomic Clock Brewing 
 Co\, located at 501 Washington St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701. Street parking and 
 parking decks are located nearby. \n\nIf you have any accessibility 
 questions or accommodation needs\, please contact us at 
 Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at least 3 business 
 days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best accommodations 
 possible.\n\n
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Other, STEAM, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-16834402
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16834402
END:VEVENT
