BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260610T170000Z
DTEND:20260610T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260610T000000Z
SUMMARY:Daytime Book Club: The Night Watchman
DESCRIPTION:Come join the Daytime Book Club as we discuss this month's 
 book! New members are always welcome (we love meeting new people!). 
 Registration is appreciated but not required.\n\nThis month we will discuss 
 The Night Watchman by Louise Erdrich. The description for the book is 
 below:\n"It is 1953. Thomas Wazhushk is the night watchman at the first 
 factory to open near the Turtle Mountain Reservation in rural North Dakota. 
 He is also a prominent Chippewa Council member\, trying to understand a new 
 bill that is soon to be put before Congress. The US Government calls it an 
 'emancipation' bill\; but it isn't about freedom - it threatens the rights 
 of Native Americans to their land\, their very identity. How can he fight 
 this betrayal?\n\nUnlike most of the girls on the reservation\, Pixie - 
 'Patrice' - Paranteau has no desire to wear herself down on a husband and 
 kids. She works at the factory\, earning barely enough to support her 
 mother and brother\, let alone her alcoholic father who sometimes returns 
 home to bully her for money. But Patrice needs every penny to get if she's 
 ever going to get to Minnesota to find her missing sister Vera."\n\nWe look 
 forward to seeing you all soon!\n\n\nInterested in attending a future 
 Daytime Book Club meeting? Take a look at our reading list below:\n\nMay 
 2026: To the Lighthouse by Virginia Woolf\n\nJune 2026: The Night Watchman 
 by Louise Erdrich\n\nJuly 2026: A Marriage at Sea by Sophie 
 Elmhirst\n\nAugust 2026: My Friends by Fredrik Backman\n\nSeptember 2026: 
 Wild Dark Shore by Charlotte McConaghy\n\nOctober 2026: The House on Mango 
 Street by Sandra Cisneros\n\nNovember 2026: Midnight in the Garden of Good 
 and Evil by John Berendt\n\nDecember 2026: Orbital by Samantha 
 Harvey\n\nJanuary 2027: What We Can Know by Ian McEwan\n\nFebruary 2027: 
 Song of Solomon by Toni Morrison\n\nMarch 2027: Proud Shoes by Pauli 
 Murray\n\nApril 2027: Isola by Allegra Goodman
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-14288-16576123
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16576123
END:VEVENT
