SUMMARY:Piedmont Wildlife Visit @ North Regional
DESCRIPTION:Learn about the natural history (predator/prey interactions\, 
 diet\, habitat\, adaptations including defense mechanisms) of the animals 
 as well as conservation practices for native NC wildlife. This program will 
 take place on Thursday\, June 11\, 2026 from 10-10:30 a.m. at North 
 Regional Library. The address is 221 Milton Rd. Durham\, NC 27712.\n\nThis 
 program is best for school-aged children. This program includes live 
 animals\, and a liability waiver will need to be signed by people who are 
 registered for the program. \n\nRegistration for this event is required. 
 There is a total of 55 seats available. When registering\, please remember 
 to include all people in your party I i.e. guardian and child.) Due to 
 space limitations and safety of people and animals\, those who are not 
 registered will be unable to attend.  \n\nThis event will be held system 
 wide.  If this program is full\, please check the calendar for other dates 
 and times. Thank you! \n\n \n\n \n\nQuestions? Please contact Molly at 
 mschaefer@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Molly Schaefer":MAILTO:mschaefer@dconc.gov
