BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260613T133000Z
DTEND:20260613T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20260613T000000Z
SUMMARY:Friends of the Durham Library Summer Reading Pop-Up Book Sale
DESCRIPTION:As part of the Summer Reading Kickoff\, the Friends of the 
 Durham Library will conduct a book sale in the Auditorium at the Main 
 Library on Saturday\, June 13.\n\nWe'll have a wide variety of children's 
 books for between $1 and $3. \n\nFor grown-ups\, we'll have fiction books 
 in all their variety - general fiction\, mysteries\, romance\, 
 science-fiction/fantasy/horror\, short stories\, and young adult books. 
 Hardcover books are $5 each\, while softcover books are $3 each. Types of 
 payment accepted - credit/debit card\, cash\, checks and Apple Pay. 
 \n\nCome unearth a story! \n\nParking is available in the library lot or at 
 the North Queen Street Garage which is locate at 115 North Queen Street 
 which is located directly across the street from the library. Parking is 
 free in the garage. Bring your parking ticket to a library service point 
 for validation.   \n\nThe Friends of the Durham Library is an all-volunteer 
 501(c)(3) non-profit organization that supports Durham County Library with 
 continuing education scholarships for staff\, grant funding for programs 
 and events\, and other forms of staff support. They accept donations of 
 CDs\, DVDs\, books\, puzzles\, and games which they then sort and sell back 
 to the community. For more information about the Friends and how you can 
 get involved\, please visit FODLNC.org. \n\n
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Abigail Mondragon":MAILTO:vasmondragon@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Announcements, Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-16723244
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16723244
END:VEVENT
