SUMMARY:"The Great Debaters" (2007) Film Screening
DESCRIPTION:"The Great Debaters" is a 2007 American historical drama film 
 following the trials and tribulations of the debate team of Wiley College\, 
 a historically black college. Based on a true story set in 1935 Texas 
 during the era of Jim Crow laws that haunted African Americans in the 
 American South\, this film explores the racial social issues of the Great 
 Depression and the importance of critical thinking\, education\, and 
 mentorship.
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Career Development, Movie
