SUMMARY:SCORE presents: Introduction to Recordkeeping
DESCRIPTION:YOU MUST REGISTER VIA SCORE'S LINK\n\nLast opportunity to take 
 this class until fall! \n\nSCORE Chapel Hill Durham is excited to introduce 
 a workshop for new entrepreneurs or anyone else in need of learning simple 
 record keeping. This course is a hands-on lecture/lab that teaches business 
 owners how to track their cash disbursements and receipts in a simple 
 manner to keep track of profitability on a consistent basis.\n\nThe 
 workshop requires each student to bring their own laptop computer to the 
 classroom\, and have Microsoft Excel loaded onto the computer and 
 functioning properly. A basic understanding of how to use Excel and enter 
 information into a spreadsheet is required to attend. \n\nThe workshop will 
 be taught by Ms.Camille Blommer\, a certified instructor for SCORE\, and 
 CPA who holds a Masters in Accountancy..\n\nMs. Blommer will email you the 
 two MS Excel templates/schedules that you will need to have for the class. 
 Students must register via the SCORE link provided at least two days before 
 the class to enable Ms. Blommer time to send you the two schedules and have 
 time to download onto your own laptop computer. There is no fee for the 
 class.\n\nSeating is limited —maximum attendees will be 15.
LOCATION:Meeting Room #4347\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jana Bradley":MAILTO:jbradley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development, Finance, Low Sensory Stimulation
