SUMMARY:Get Ready\, Get Set\, Let's Read: Kindergarten Kickstart Edition
DESCRIPTION:Ms. Patty & Ms. Sara are here to help prepare your Talker (kids 
 ages 4-5) as they begin the process of learning to read. Songs\, stories\, 
 and activity stations will prepare both the caregiver and the child for 
 success in school. Classes are held on Monday\, June 22nd and Monday\, July 
 27th at 11:00am at the East Regional Library. You only need to attend one 
 class. \n\nEach child will receive a bag filled with early literacy tools 
 to use at home as they continue the path to becoming a reader. \n\nFor 
 children ages 4-5 years old. To help us manage space\, please register only 
 the child participating in the storytime. Adults are not counted in 
 registration.\n\nThis initiative is made possible from the generous support 
 of the Durham Library Foundation.
LOCATION:East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Sara Gibson":MAILTO:sgibson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Community Engagement, Durham Library Foundation, Story Time
