SUMMARY:Unearth Geodes
DESCRIPTION:Explore geodes in this hands-on tween program inspired by the 
 Summer Reading theme “Unearth a Story." We’ll start by learning what 
 geodes are and how they form. Participants will then take part in a 
 crystal‑growing simulation experiment\, creating their own crystal 
 formations to mirror the natural process. Finally\, the adventure continues 
 as everyone cracks open rocks. Will yours be a geode filled with dazzling 
 crystals? There’s only one way to find out!\n\nRegistration is required. 
 Geared towards ages 8-13\, siblings welcome. Children under age 11 must 
 have a parent/guardian accompanying them.\n\nNote: If you have any 
 accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, please contact us at 
 Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made at least 3 business 
 days prior to the event to ensure we can provide the best accommodations 
 possible!
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:STEAM, Summer Reading
