SUMMARY:Space Agriculture - A Simulation in Stations
DESCRIPTION:What's it like to research plant life and try to garden in 
 outer space on a space station?\n\nJoin the Maker   STEAM team to explore 4 
 stations of short activities simulating parts of what space research about 
 agriculture\, plants\, and gardening looks like on a space station. In 
 these stations\, you can use NASA information to:\n\n\n	\n	Pick a (pretend) 
 plant to grow\n	\n	\n	Set up the growing environment\n	\n	\n	"Water" the 
 plant\n	\n	\n	Measure the plant's growth\n	\n\n\nEach of these stations 
 will be simulations\, no actual planting occurring this time! These 
 activities are geared towards ages 5 and up\, all ages welcome.\n\nThis 
 program is drop-in\, no registration required. Please join us between 5pm 
 and 6pm in the Innovation Lab on 3rd floor of Main Library. The stations 
 will take most participants around 20 to 30 minutes to complete. This event 
 is for all ages\; children under age 11 must be accompanied by an adult. 
 \n\nThis program is a precursor to the Space Farms program occurring in the 
 Main Auditorium on this same date from 6-7:30pm.  Please register for the 
 auditorium program here.\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that all requests be made at least 3 business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible.
LOCATION:Innovation Lab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, High Sensory Stimulation, Maker, STEAM
UID:LibCal-14288-16903770
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16903770
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260624T220000Z
DTEND:20260624T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260624T000000Z
SUMMARY:Finance Book Club - Personal Branding for Introverts
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Finance Book Club\, a book club focused on finance\, 
 the world economy\, and everything in between. Join to delve into 
 thoughtful discussions about the forces impacting our world today. For this 
 month's meeting\, we'll be going over Personal Branding for Introverts by 
 Goldie Chan. Bring your thoughts and reflections!\n\n"To build a career\, 
 you need a personal brand to showcase your distinct skills\, experience\, 
 and expertise. Building that brand can feel daunting—particularly for 
 introverts. Conventional wisdom holds that introverts should fake 
 extroversion in order to succeed\, advice that can be terrifying for anyone 
 who finds social interaction exhausting. Personal branding expert and 
 introvert Goldie Chan says it doesn’t have to be this way.\n\nChan 
 empowers introverts to create memorable and recognizable personal brands 
 without feeling the pressure to become someone else. With examples from 
 everyday introverts to introvert celebrities like Taylor Swift and LeVar 
 Burton\, Chan shows how introversion can be a superpower when building a 
 personal brand. She shares strategies for goal setting\, navigating 
 in-person networking events\, building online and offline communities\, 
 partnering effectively with extroverts\, and sustaining energy for the long 
 run.\n\nThis book is essential reading for any introvert looking to level 
 up a career or community without sacrificing authenticity."
LOCATION:Meeting Room #4311\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Business, Career Development, Finance
UID:LibCal-14288-16949176
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16949176
END:VEVENT
