SUMMARY:Sculpt What You Hear - A Musical and Artistic Relaxation Program
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for a creative adventure where music\, imagination\, 
 and dinosaurs collide! As part of our Summer Reading theme “Unearth Your 
 Story\,” join us for a one-of-a-kind hands-on experience where you’ll 
 sculpt what you hear while enjoying the sounds of a live saxophonist\, 
 DSquared.\n\nAs the music fills the room\, let the rhythms and melodies 
 guide your creativity. Using clay\, participants will shape their own 
 dinosaurs\, fossils\, landscapes\, or imaginative creations inspired by the 
 sounds around them. Will the music inspire a roaring T-Rex\, a peaceful 
 prehistoric valley\, or a fossil waiting to be discovered? There’s only 
 one way to find out.\n\nThis relaxed and engaging program is perfect for 
 anyone who loves art\, music\, dinosaurs\, or simply trying something new. 
 Come dig into your creativity\, follow the music\, and unearth your story 
 one sculpture at a time.
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Alexandra Wurst":MAILTO:awurst@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Business, Community Engagement, Durham, Music, Social, Summer Reading
