DTSTAMP:20260624T000000Z
SUMMARY:Networking for Introverts: Unleashing Your SUPERPOWER
DESCRIPTION:If the idea of a "mixer" makes you want to find that quiet 
 corner seat next to the snacks and stay there\, welcome home. Most 
 networking advice uses a one-size-fits-all approach that doesn't always 
 account for how we're wired.\n\nThis is for the rest of us—the 
 observers\, the listeners\, and those who notice the small details others 
 might miss. We aren’t here to change who you are\; we’re here to help 
 you activate your natural traits and turn them into your greatest 
 professional asset. \n\nWho Should Be There:\n\n\n	Early in your career: 
 Learn the "cheat codes" to networking before you burn out trying to play a 
 character that isn't you.\n	The "Curious" (Nosey) Extroverts: We see you. 
 Come see how we navigate the world \n	The Workforce Folks: You want to find 
 real talent? Stop looking at the loudest person and start looking at the 
 one who’s actually processing the data.\n\n\nThe "Business Whisperer" 
 Reality Check: We’re going deep into the science of why our brains work 
 differently. It’s not "shyness"—it’s Business Intelligence.\n\n⚠️ 
 SPOILER ALERT: This is a live session. We’re doing 
 Intro’speriments.\n\n\n	Pro-Tip: Show up early. Scout your seat. Get 
 settled. We’re going to practice networking in a way that doesn’t drain 
 you.\n\n\n \n\n \n\nJacinta Walker's Bio: The Business Whisperer\n\nI’m a 
 professional growth architect and strategic consultant with 25 years of 
 experience mastering the "Invisible Edge." People call me the Business 
 Whisperer and the Networking Queen\, which is a bit of a paradox: I’m a 
 high-functioning introvert who can work a room better than most 
 extroverts.\n\nThe Secret? I’m not playing a character—I’m activating 
 my observation skills. While everyone else focuses on the noise\, I listen 
 for what isn't being said.\n\nWhy No One Believes I’m an Introvert: If 
 you’ve seen me on stage at 1 Million Cups or leading a session at the 
 Durham Tech\, you’d think I was born for the spotlight. But I’ll be the 
 first to tell you that after a day of "Real Talking\," my only goal is a 
 nap to recharge. I don’t see introversion as a barrier\; I see it as a 
 SUPERPOWER for deep connection and strategic business intelligence.\n\n\n\n
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Ciera Williams":MAILTO:cbwilliams@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development
UID:LibCal-14288-16562388
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16562388
END:VEVENT
