SUMMARY:Homeschool Learning Lab: Fizzy Dinosaur Eggs
DESCRIPTION:ROARRR into science! Discover chemical reactions with a 
 hands-on sensory STEM activity. Learn about acids and bases while creating 
 your own dinosaur eggs. \n\nWeather permitting\, this activity will be 
 outside. This activity will include ingredients such as baking soda\, 
 vinegar Please wear clothes you don't mind getting messy.\n\n Homeschool 
 Learning Lab is a weekly program that offers engaging enrichment lessons 
 created just for homeschoolers.  Come join us each week to learn\, 
 explore\, and connect with other homeschooling families in Durham. \n\nFor 
 any questions regarding kit pickup or accommodation needs\, please reach 
 out to Molly at mschaefer@dconc.gov.  We ask that all requests be made at 
 least three (3) business days prior to the event to ensure we can provide 
 the best accommodations possible!\n\nProgram details: \n\nDate: Thursday\, 
 June 25\, 2026 \n\nTime: 10a.m.\n\nLocation: North Regional 
 Library\n\nAddress: 221 Milton Rd. Durham\, NC 27712. \n\n
